  "body": "Found while working #35 (pocket/slot recognition).\n\n**What happens:** a typed 2D Slot whose cutter reaches its round cap is reported as a gouge on every cutting move, with no part model in the document at all, so its path never posts.\n\n**Reproduced on `main` 7e907afa** (headless, app layer): new world, `SetStock` box 80 x 60 x 20, `AddTool` `EM-0600-4FL`, `CreateOperation` Slot on `SrcRef::Stock` with `a = (-15, 0)`, `b = (15, 0)`, `top_z` fixed 20, `bottom_z` fixed 10, stepdown 5, then `GenerateOperation`:\n- width 6 (cutter = width, one pass along the centreline): `Gouge` at moves 2, 3, 7, 8, 12, 13 (the plunge and the feed of every level);\n- width 10 (rings at +-2): `Gouge` on every feed of every level.\n\n**Likely cause (not confirmed):** the Slot's machining region is `operation::stadium(a, b, width / 2)` with `CAP_SEGMENTS = 16` chords per semicircle, inscribed in the true arc. The tangency law (b) in `crates/sim/src/verify/section.rs` wants d(centre, boundary) >= r - tol with `GOUGE_TOL = 0.01`, but a centre on the cap's centre sits only r * cos(5.625 deg) from a chord: 3 mm cutter radius -> 2.9855 < 2.99, a 0.0145 mm \"bite\" that is pure chord error. The generator's passes ride the true arc, so the verdict convicts a tangent cutter.\n\n**Done means:** a Slot whose passes are tangent to its own stadium verifies clean (no `Gouge`), while a Slot driven past its walls still does; pinned by a test that generates the width-6 and width-10 cases above and asserts no `Gouge`, plus one oversize case that is still convicted.\n\nRelated: #35's recognised slots create Slot operations and inherit this until it is fixed (their tests pin the path geometry exactly instead of the verifier's verdict).\n",
